  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and seasonable conditions continue through \nearly next week, with frost possible this weekend.\n\nSurface high pressure remains to the north through Saturday with\ndry and seasonable conditions expected to continue. Tonight's\nlow temperatures will be in the upper 30s to 40s. For Friday \nand Saturday, surface high pressure extends southward from \nCanada with dry cold fronts bringing in cooler air. High \ntemperatures stay in the 50s to low 60s while overnight lows \nplummet into the 30s for most. The exception will be east of the\nI-95 corridor where low temperatures stay in the low 40s. Frost\nis possible Friday night and Saturday night. \n\nHigh pressure will continue to build southward into the region \nSunday through Tuesday. Dry conditions and seasonable \ntemperatures expected each day with light north to east winds. A\nbackdoor cold front could try to push into the region Tuesday \ninto Tuesday night, but will have very little to no moisture \nwith it to produce any precipitation. A surge of cooler \ntemperatures will follow behind the front for the day on \nWednesday.",
